-- title:
--   Universal property of the crossing quotient W[X₀,X₁]/(X₀X₁-t)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ and $S$ be commutative rings, let $\iota\colon W\to S$ be a ring homomorphism, let $t\in W$, and let $x,y\in S$ satisfy $x\,y=\iota(t)$. Write $\mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\,W\,t$ for the quotient of the polynomial ring $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$ in two variables $X_0,X_1$ over $W$ by the ideal generated by the single element $X_0X_1-C(t)$, regarded as a $W$-algebra through the structure map $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,W\,(\mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\,W\,t)$, and let `CrossingQuotient.U t` and `CrossingQuotient.V t` be the two distinguished elements of this quotient, which the proof handles as the residue classes of the variables $X_0$ and $X_1$. The assertion is that there exists exactly one ring homomorphism $\chi\colon \mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\,W\,t\to S$ such that the structure map $W\to\mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\,W\,t$ followed by $\chi$ equals $\iota$, and $\chi(\,$`CrossingQuotient.U t`$\,)=x$ and $\chi(\,$`CrossingQuotient.V t`$\,)=y$. Uniqueness is asserted in the strong form of `ExistsUnique`: any ring homomorphism with these three properties coincides with the one produced.
--
--   This is the universal property of the local model of a plane crossing (node): $S$-points of $\operatorname{Spec} W[u,v]/(uv-t)$ over $\iota$ correspond to factorisations $xy=\iota(t)$ in $S$. It is used in the computation of the Krull dimension of the stalks of the crossing scheme and in the local analysis of the model of the modular curve at a node, where the relevant points are pairs $(p^e/c,\,c)$.
